  "notes": "なさる is the honorific ({尊敬語|そんけいご}) form of する. Use it when describing the actions of someone you wish to show respect toward.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]をなさる\n\nKEIGO SYSTEM FOR する:\n- {尊敬語|そんけいご} (honorific): なさる — for the other person's actions\n- {謙譲語|けんじょうご} (humble): いたす — for your own actions\n- {丁寧語|ていねいご} (polite): します\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- どうなさいましたか: What happened? / What's wrong? (polite)\n- ご{注文|ちゅうもん}はお{決|き}まりになさいましたか: Have you decided on your order?\n- お{好|す}きなようになさってください: Please do as you like",
